{
  "protocol": "Experiment: does a SHAP-guided look-alike specialist improve the SVM?\n\nIdea: the SVM is the one main model. When its top two guesses are a known\nlook-alike pair, a small binary SVM for that pair makes the final call, using\nonly the regions of the character that SHAP says separate the pair.\n\nEverything is chosen on TRAINING data, using out-of-fold predictions:\n  * which pairs count as look-alikes,\n  * which regions each specialist uses,\n  * whether each specialist is kept at all.\nThe test set is only scored at the very end.\n\nOutput: results/metrics/lookalike_experiment.json\n",
